# ==============================================================================
# Node 18 (languages/node/Dockerfile.alpine) — ACCEPTED RESIDUAL RISK
#
# Scope: node:18-alpine ONLY. Node 20/22/24/26 images are not affected.
# Root cause: dependencies vendored inside the npm CLI itself
# (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules), shipped by the final npm@10
# release (npm 10.9.9). The npm@10 line receives no further updates and npm 11+
# requires Node >= 20, so these findings are UNFIXABLE while Node 18 remains in
# matrix.json — Node 18 has been EOL upstream since 2025-04-30.
#
# Affected vendored packages / findings:
#   brace-expansion 2.0.2          -> CVE-2026-13149, CVE-2026-14257, CVE-2026-69152
#   ip-address 10.1.0              -> CVE-2026-69192
#   pacote 19.0.2 / 20.0.1         -> CVE-2026-9496 (2 findings)
#   picomatch 4.0.3                -> CVE-2026-33671
#   sigstore 3.1.0                 -> CVE-2026-48815
# (4 MEDIUM + 1 LOW findings remain visible — below the CRITICAL/HIGH gate.)
#
# RE-REVIEW: remove these entries as soon as Node 18 is dropped from
# matrix.json, or if npm@10 ever publishes a release with patched deps.
# ==============================================================================
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-9496
CVE-2026-33671
CVE-2026-48815
